      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Method",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Mix the pork mince with half the shallots, half the garlic, 1 tbsp fish sauce, and 1 tbsp sugar. Shape into small patties about 4 cm across. Chill for 30 minutes.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Mix the pork belly slices with the remaining shallots, garlic, 1 tbsp fish sauce, and 1 tbsp sugar. Toss to coat and leave to marinate while the patties chill.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Make the dipping broth. Mix the remaining fish sauce and sugar with the lime juice and 200 ml of warm water. Add the sliced chilli. Taste and balance if needed.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Heat a griddle pan or grill to high. Cook the pork patties for 3 to 4 minutes per side until charred and cooked through.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cook the pork belly slices on the same griddle for 2 to 3 minutes per side until lightly charred.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Divide the warm dipping broth between 4 bowls. Add some pork patties and pork belly slices to each bowl.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Serve the cold noodles, fresh herbs, and bean sprouts on the side. Diners dip the noodles into the broth and eat everything together.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          }
        ],
        "type": "orderedList"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Chill the shaped patties for at least 30 minutes before grilling. Handle them as little as possible when turning.",
              "cause": "The mixture was too wet or not chilled enough.",
              "symptom": "The pork patties fall apart on the grill."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Add more warm water a tablespoon at a time until the flavour is balanced. The broth should be savoury but light.",
              "cause": "The ratio of fish sauce to water is off.",
              "symptom": "The dipping broth tastes too salty."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Pork belly cooks quickly when sliced thin. Two to three minutes per side is enough. Remove as soon as the fat crisps.",
              "cause": "They were grilled for too long.",
              "symptom": "The pork belly slices are dry and tough."
            }
          }
        ],
        "type": "troubleshooter"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Where this dish lives",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Bun cha is a dish of Hanoi, the capital of northern Vietnam. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "It is sold at street stalls throughout the city, especially at lunchtime. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "The dish became internationally famous after an American president ate it at a Hanoi street stall in 2016. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Unlike pho, bun cha is not widely eaten outside the north. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Hanoi locals are proud of it and consider it one of the city's signature dishes.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      }
    ],
    "type": "doc"
  },
  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "definition": "In Vietnamese cooking, chả refers to a pork preparation that can be a patty, sausage, or ground meat mixture that is grilled or fried.",
      "term": "Chả",
